<title>GERMANY: German passenger traffic grows 11.5pct in April 97.</title>
<headline>German passenger traffic grows 11.5pct in April 97.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German air traffic rose strongly in April with an 11.5 percent growth to more than 9.7 million passengers, the German airports association ADV said.</p>
<p>The passenger market grew 4.4 percent over the first four months of 1997, reflecting a recovery after a slow start to the year, the latest ADV traffic report showed.</p>
<p>The main factors behind the April pick-up were a 17 percent rise in domestic air travel and 12 percent growth in intercontinental traffic.</p>
<p>Fastest-growing major airports last month were Duesseldorf, Munich and Hamburg. Details with percentage changes from last year include:</p>
<p>					   April	     Pct change</p>
<p>    Total			    9,778,013	    Up   11.5</p>
<p>    Domestic			 3,130,080	    Up   17.0</p>
<p>    Europe			   4,836,032	    Up    8.4</p>
<p>    Overseas			 1,662,063	    Up   12.1</p>
<p>    Transit			    138,686	    Down  0.9</p>
<p>					Jan-Apr 97	   Pct change</p>
<p>    Total			   34,284,504	    Up    4.4</p>
<p>    Domestic			11,417,786	    Up    2.0</p>
<p>    Europe			  16,095,536	    Up    4.6</p>
<p>    Overseas			 6,179,663	    Up    9.0</p>
<p>    Transit			    560,315	    Up    2.0</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
